   "lines": [
    "Went to Church. In",
    "afternoon took a",
    "long tramp with",
    "Jack. He is the",
    "best companion",
    "on a trip of this",
    "kind I know.",
    "I always enjoy",
    "these winter excursions",
    "to Oyster Bay so",
    "much. The shooting",
    "though very poor",
    "is great fun, and",
    "after the cold",
    "and fatigue, of the",
    "day, one appreciates",
    "so a warm supper and",
    "rousing wood fire.",
    "Snowed in the night"
   ],
